  m_Name: FarmStick_Excavator_Right_Default
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_displayName: FarmStick Excavator Right Default
  m_setupNotes: 'Template profile for Thrustmaster SimTask FarmStick.

    Official
    hardware mapping exposes 33 buttons and 8 axes: Axis 1/2 main stick, Axis 3 twist,
    Axis 4/5 mini-stick, Axis 6/7/8 thumb controls.

    This Linux default
    profile uses the control names currently reported by Unity Input System:
    Stick/x, Stick/y, RotateX, RotateY, Throttle and Rudder.

    Current
    excavator routing is aligned to the real machine: the swing/stick side uses
    an inverted Y for swing and an inverted X for stick, while the boom/bucket
    side uses Y for boom and an inverted X for bucket.

    In dual-FarmStick mode that means left
    main Y->Swing (inverted), left main X->Stick (inverted), right main Y->Boom,
    right main X->Bucket (inverted).

    If your platform reports different control names,
    use the diagnostics menu to inspect the live controls and retarget the bindings.

    The default excavator travel mapping uses the two rocker axes in Work mode:
    Axis 7 (Throttle) for Drive and Axis 8 (Rudder) for Steer.

    Switch
    the FarmStick to Work mode if you want analog rocker axes; in Drive mode
    those controls become buttons 27-30 and Linux may not expose them individually.

    The FarmStick MODE button is official button 31. On Linux it may appear
    as an Unknown button or may not be exposed; this profile defaults the software
    stick-mode switch to Unknown so you can test that path quickly.

    When
    the stick-mode switch is active in single-device mode, the main stick and
    mini-stick roles are swapped while preserving that same Y/X excavator mapping.

    Reset Episode defaults to ''base5'', which is intended to be a spare
    base button on the generic joystick layout. If your platform reports different
    button names, use the diagnostics menu to inspect the live controls and retarget
    the reset binding.

    Start/stop episode buttons stay disabled by
    default because Unity''s Linux joystick layout does not expose the FarmStick''s
    official button 19-33 numbering consistently across machines.

    Run
    Thrustmaster hardware calibration first; use this profile only for residual deadzone,
    inversion and range tuning.'
  m_manufacturerContains: Thrustmaster
  m_productContains: SimTask FarmStick
